			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837247">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>The SCP is a video game cartridge with scratched up stickers and scratched logo and title which is impossible to make out.</li>
<li>a video game cartridge that can be played on Nintendo 64, but no one<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-261084-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-261084-1')">1</a></sup> remembers or knows about the game or the development of the game.</li>
<li>whenever a player dies in the video game, within 24 hours the player in real life would face the same fate as the player who died in the video game.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The whole idea of this SCP is that the game kills the subject the way the subject died in the video game.</p>
<p>When the cartridge is plugged into a regular Nintendo 64, the player will be introduced into an open-world. The place that sets the player in a city called: &quot;Alt City&quot;, the player inside the game can virtually do ANYTHING<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-261084-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-261084-2')">2</a></sup>. The more the player plays in the city, the more the player wants to commit violence.</p>
<p>Whenever the player dies in the game then the tv unknowingly shuts off with no solutions fixing it. Within 24 hours the player will die in real life in the same way the player died in the game. There is no other way of avoiding death, and any attempts avoiding the death would just lead to death.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> What is special about this SCP is because I think (I THINK! I am not certain) that this SCP is the first video game that kills anyone. (Again, I am not certain, there is probably an SCP like this. I don't know&#8230;)</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I would <strong>LOVE</strong> to see some criticism or feedback. Thank you!</p>
