<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> History, Action</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Documentation and Experiment Logs</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
*Miniature Medieval Europe made out of paper.<br />
*Inhabited by mini satient paper beings<br />
*There are wars and conquests.<br />
*Can communicate with humans.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Field agents found a miniature castle made entirely out of white paper in the basement of an old building. They bring it back as a present for a foundation scientist. The scientist discovered one day that the castle was filled with little talking paper people. They interview the supposed &quot;king&quot; of this land. The castle slowly expands larger and larger, with more and more people. This scientist then proposes to make this an SCP which is granted. The tiny people refer to the scientist as their god. When a researcher accidentally brought in a red paper for unknown reasons, the red paper duplicated and became a separate empire that was enemies with the white paper empire. They are now stored separately.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I don't think something like this have ever been done before. It is an very interesting topic to see paper people going about their day.</p>
